WEBVTT

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:04.771
The undefeated champion,
the White Wind, a.k.a. Gerd Frentzen,

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:08.104
is putting on a show
at the start of this race, too!

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:38.130
What the...?

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.248
- Someone's lying in here!
- Eh?!

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.116
Shut off the alarm!

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.787
Can't hear you!

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.055
It's a naked lady!

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.558
- You shitting me?!
- You can too hear me!

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:01.561
Hey, check out her EKG! I think she's dead!

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.296
You're right!

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.397
She's dead!

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.199
This is an incident! We gotta report it!

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.168
But shut off that alarm first!

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.769
I think it'll shut off if you close the door!

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.737
You could've said so sooner!

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.777
- What're you doing?!
- The tray fell, that's all!

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:21.481
Quit staring at the
naked chick and cover her up!

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.608
I ain't staring!

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:29.422
Nishii, the Japanese Hope,
passes lgor to boldly take on the champ!

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:33.518
Oh! He slid off the track! Is he all right?!

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:46.239
Main gate ambulance,
requesting confirmation. A dead body...

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.240
It's awake!

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.876
- What is?
- The body!

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:53.676
D-Demoniac sighted!
Request immediate XAT assistance!

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.304
Something's happened!

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.865
A runaway car has busted onto
the track and is going the wrong way!

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.145
An ambulance?!

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:33.379
O-Oh no! The runaway
vehicle is headed for the pits!

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:59.772
Something is emerging
from the...! I-It's a Demoniac!

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.412
Stop!

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:14.590
Damn monster!

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.586
Get out of there, Gerd!

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.660
All police, lead the civilians away!

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.496
Do not let them near the Amalgam!

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:53.499
Heavy artillery is out of
the question in this situation.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.335
I'll go.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:58.805
I'll take it down with dumdum
bullets from point-blank range.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.966
I'll back you up!

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.831
Now what's this machine?!

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.610
What are these things?!

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:03.403
You okay? You were having a nightmare.

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.064
Hermann...

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:09.309
You're here again?

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.744
You're not turning me away today?

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:14.080
No, I am.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:19.052
Come on, Gerd! That tone reminds
me of flat beer! Snap out of it!

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:23.556
A racer who can't ride
is worth less than flat beer...

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.426
I might as well be dead.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:29.395
You're not dead! You're alive!

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.931
Just so you know, there won't be any miracles.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:33.599
The doctor assures me of it.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:36.102
I'm well aware of that!

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:41.441
Then quit with the sympathy
and leave. You must be busy.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:46.112
I wanted to return the
words you gave me back then.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.947
Back then?

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:52.008
You told me there was a path out there for me.

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:56.522
Five years ago, I fell
from second rider to third

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.991
when lgor beat me in his rookie year.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:02.662
I kept to the racetrack anyway,
despite sensing my limit.

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:05.698
That's when you told me.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:08.801
I'm fired?! Are you telling
me to give up racing?!

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:13.506
I'll be frank. You lack
the kind of strength lgor has.

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:16.709
Plus, regulations are
changing starting next season.

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:20.980
It's not about skill.
You're too straightforward and kind.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:26.486
To compete in races, you need
the strength to be cruel and brutal.

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:29.155
Find your path, Hermann.

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:34.727
Use your skill and absurdly
straightforward character to their fullest.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.829
No matter how much
of a rut you think you're in,

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.059
there is a path out there for you.

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:44.835
And then I quit racing.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:50.476
I was depressed for a while after.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:53.613
I must've still had some regrets.

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:58.518
There was even a short time
when I thought you said all that

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:02.855
just to get rid of an up-and-comer.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:05.992
But after I found the path
that is the Mobile Traffic Unit,

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:08.861
I've always been grateful to you.

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:10.196
You're the one who said

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:12.999
there's a path out there,
no matter how much of a rut you're in!

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.524
So...

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:19.105
...don't talk about being dead!

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:23.166
I won't give up! I will find a path!

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.616
I never could've told you this
when we used to race together,

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:33.519
but you were my hero.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:35.888
That's no different now.

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:37.446
I'll be back later.

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:43.696
Sorry to do this during a patrol, Amanda.

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:45.965
He was a close friend of yours.

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:50.732
I owe him my life. There'll never
be another racer as talented as him.

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:55.641
He'll stand up. Gerd will live again.

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:57.666
You really believe in him.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:26.539
Five of those injured in last
month's race incident died yesterday,

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:28.074
and ten have died today.

00:08:28.074 --> 00:08:32.211
The day of the incident, nine died,
forty were seriously injured,

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:34.714
and twenty suffered light injuries.

00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:39.118
It can't be a viral infection.
They've all been tested.

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:42.288
What about the analysis
data from that Amalgam?

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:43.556
But, Boss!

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:46.792
There are still so many unknowns
when it comes to Amalgams!

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:49.095
It might as well be demonic possession!

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:51.564
What we know is that corpses become active,

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:54.100
assimilate with things, and attack people.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:58.137
Except this time, an Amalgam
attacked another Amalgam.

00:08:58.137 --> 00:09:00.873
It's not much, but it only deepens the mystery.

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:04.544
Not just that! It amalgamated
with a car and motorcycle instantly!

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:06.145
Never mind that!

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:10.616
We had all the gates sealed,
so why couldn't we find the other one?!

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:11.284
Boss!

00:09:11.284 --> 00:09:15.121
We've detected signs of an
Amalgam in a Lathen warehouse district!

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:16.554
Okay! Let's move out!

00:09:21.561 --> 00:09:27.800
The White Wind, Gerd Frentzen,
conquered every track out there.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:31.671
Has there ever been such a talented racer?

00:09:31.671 --> 00:09:36.008
Every course he ran
was always blessed by God.

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:39.579
Indeed, he was a miraculously talented racer.

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:42.715
It's truly regrettable that his
unfortunate accident occurred.

00:09:42.715 --> 00:09:43.849
Jil...

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:45.718
Hello, this is Jil Hoffmann.

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:48.921
However, Gerd Frentzen
is an undefeated legend.

00:09:48.921 --> 00:09:52.692
Let's have faith that he will
rise above this unfortunate incident

00:09:52.692 --> 00:09:56.253
and return to the racetrack once more.

00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:04.337
After our analysis, it's been
36 hours since the incident here.

00:10:04.337 --> 00:10:09.241
Alright. We'll end the lockdown
12 hours after our investigation.

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:12.044
It really tore up the place again...

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:14.814
- Witnesses?
- None.

00:10:14.814 --> 00:10:18.150
The chance of it coming
back here is slim to none.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:24.056
Meaning all we can do is wait
for it to make a move, like always.

00:10:24.056 --> 00:10:26.726
I see someone on the far
end of the warehouse district.

00:10:26.726 --> 00:10:28.060
Who's closest?

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.262
Amanda. She's outside the gate.

00:10:30.262 --> 00:10:31.964
Send her there.

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:34.767
Amanda. I see someone at Point B7.

00:10:34.767 --> 00:10:37.903
It could be a witness. Please make contact.

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:39.234
Roger.

00:10:43.142 --> 00:10:47.113
There we are. Making contact!

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:50.173
Excuse me! I'd like to ask you...!

00:10:56.656 --> 00:10:58.123
It disappeared...

00:11:07.733 --> 00:11:09.701
You alive?

00:11:12.672 --> 00:11:14.674
Gerd...

00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:17.700
There's a path, right?

00:11:20.212 --> 00:11:22.882
Are you okay to go on your own?

00:11:22.882 --> 00:11:23.949
Yeah.

00:11:23.949 --> 00:11:28.254
Everyone on the team'll
be happy to see you back.

00:11:28.254 --> 00:11:30.690
So will your girlfriend.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:35.094
I haven't seen Jil in a while.
I was in pretty bad shape then.

00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:37.763
Go and surprise her, then.

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:38.695
Yeah.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.167
Hermann.

00:12:07.493 --> 00:12:11.297
I woulda cleaned up a little
if I'd known you were coming!

00:12:11.297 --> 00:12:12.765
No, that's okay.

00:12:12.765 --> 00:12:15.801
You're looking better.
When did you get out of the hospital?

00:12:15.801 --> 00:12:17.870
Just today.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.905
Oh, that's good.

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:23.841
I'm sure you'll be fine.
Whatever you do will work out well.

00:12:24.977 --> 00:12:27.346
How's the team been lately?

00:12:27.346 --> 00:12:32.818
It's only been a month since what
happened. It's been utter confusion.

00:12:32.818 --> 00:12:34.754
I've been thinking, Matthew.

00:12:34.754 --> 00:12:37.848
If there's anything I can do for the team...

00:12:39.325 --> 00:12:41.761
Matthew. Those are my...

00:12:41.761 --> 00:12:43.796
Listen, Gerd...

00:12:43.796 --> 00:12:46.799
You understand, don't you?
The team's been hurting too.

00:12:46.799 --> 00:12:51.403
They don't have it in them to
leave their fallen teammate behind.

00:12:51.403 --> 00:12:55.875
Plus, I hadn't planned on telling you like this.

00:12:55.875 --> 00:13:00.146
I know discarding a hero isn't
exactly great team loyalty, but, umm...

00:13:00.146 --> 00:13:02.915
The owner says he'll talk to you

00:13:02.915 --> 00:13:05.785
about covering your
living expenses for a while...

00:13:05.785 --> 00:13:07.286
That's enough, Matthew.

00:13:07.286 --> 00:13:10.187
That's enough. I get it.

00:13:12.992 --> 00:13:15.394
Let me quit on my own.

00:13:15.394 --> 00:13:19.125
Sorry... Gerd.

00:13:21.333 --> 00:13:23.969
Did you hear? Gerd-san is being cut!

00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:25.404
It's only natural.

00:13:25.404 --> 00:13:29.108
No matter how gifted he is,
he's worth nothing if he can't ride.

00:13:29.108 --> 00:13:31.510
Luck is one part of skill, too.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:34.079
You seem happy for some reason, lgor-san.

00:13:34.079 --> 00:13:36.949
That's pretty cold, after all he's done for you.

00:13:36.949 --> 00:13:38.417
Even if it is a pity,

00:13:38.417 --> 00:13:41.887
there's no racer who wouldn't
be happy to see a top spot open up.

00:13:41.887 --> 00:13:44.490
Now I can finally ride at the lead.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:47.948
To be honest, he was an eyesore.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:13.152
I know how you must feel, Gerd Frentzen-san.

00:14:13.152 --> 00:14:15.518
You want to ride, don't you?

00:14:17.022 --> 00:14:19.425
Again, just like before.

00:14:19.425 --> 00:14:21.493
What do you...?!

00:14:21.493 --> 00:14:25.264
This is a new, as-of-yet unapproved drug.

00:14:25.264 --> 00:14:27.466
Human trials haven't finished yet, either.

00:14:27.466 --> 00:14:32.004
If it works, your body will become
even greater than it used to be.

00:14:32.004 --> 00:14:34.073
You can't be serious...

00:14:34.073 --> 00:14:36.542
But, there is a risk involved.

00:14:36.542 --> 00:14:42.948
High fever and hallucinations
caused by sudden neuronal growth...

00:14:42.948 --> 00:14:45.974
At the very worst, death is even possible.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:52.625
It's your choice to take it or not.

00:14:52.625 --> 00:14:55.294
Why are you giving me this?

00:14:55.294 --> 00:15:01.199
You seemed the most suitable to give it to...

00:15:05.037 --> 00:15:08.908
I ask that you mention this to no one.

00:15:08.908 --> 00:15:12.139
I pray you receive the saving grace of God.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:42.408
Gerd. It's me, Jil. Congratulations
on getting out of the hospital.

00:15:42.408 --> 00:15:44.643
You're really strong.

00:15:44.643 --> 00:15:48.080
I'm sure you'll be able to
pave a new life for yourself.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.950
It's just... I can't do it.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:54.019
I don't think I can stay
by your side as you are now.

00:15:54.019 --> 00:15:57.523
I'm not strong enough
to walk this path with you.

00:15:57.523 --> 00:16:03.228
I'm sorry, Gerd. I really am...

00:16:03.228 --> 00:16:06.129
Goodbye...

00:16:29.421 --> 00:16:31.156
I've caught up with the Amalgam.

00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:34.126
It was hiding, just as you anticipated, Boss.

00:16:34.126 --> 00:16:36.594
It's almost like a ninja...

00:16:39.131 --> 00:16:41.734
It stopped. Confirm the visual.

00:16:41.734 --> 00:16:47.172
It must've hid over 10 days at
the racetrack for the lockdown to end.

00:16:47.172 --> 00:16:48.607
Okay! Send out the bait!

00:16:48.607 --> 00:16:50.676
Roger!

00:16:50.676 --> 00:16:52.644
Sending the unmanned car!

00:16:52.644 --> 00:16:54.680
Al, Brad! You ready?!

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:58.384
- Locked on to its right leg!
- Locked on to its left leg!

00:16:58.384 --> 00:17:00.011
Operation commence!

00:17:07.126 --> 00:17:09.185
- Blow it!
- Roger!

00:17:16.635 --> 00:17:19.071
What's wrong?! Why hasn't it exploded?!

00:17:19.071 --> 00:17:21.440
Perhaps it fused with the detonator too?

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.808
You can't be serious!

00:17:22.808 --> 00:17:24.443
It's assimilating too fast!

00:17:24.443 --> 00:17:27.613
Hermann! Amanda! Hit it with
missiles from the front and rear!

00:17:27.613 --> 00:17:30.138
- Keep it in check!
- Got it!

00:17:47.199 --> 00:17:49.064
Missiles have impacted!

00:17:50.536 --> 00:17:54.370
Target has taken heavy damage and is on fire!

00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:02.247
Boss. Operation is complete.

00:18:02.247 --> 00:18:05.484
Okay, light it up and confirm the situation!

00:18:05.484 --> 00:18:09.352
We're locking the area
down for the next 48 hours!

00:18:29.374 --> 00:18:33.105
The press... Ah, well.

00:18:35.581 --> 00:18:37.674
Damn rubberneckers.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:44.612
It's still alive! Recommencing operation!

00:18:46.258 --> 00:18:48.249
Eight o'clock!

00:18:50.329 --> 00:18:52.194
Damn thing!

00:18:57.703 --> 00:19:00.572
What are you doing?! Shoot!

00:19:00.572 --> 00:19:03.275
Shoot, Hermann!

00:19:03.275 --> 00:19:06.369
The detonator! Everyone, hold your fire!

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:11.283
The Amalgam restarted and
is carrying the plastic explosive!

00:19:11.283 --> 00:19:14.353
Yeah, I know! Damn!

00:19:14.353 --> 00:19:16.755
Attention, helicopter. This is the XAT.

00:19:16.755 --> 00:19:22.427
We're currently in emergency
deployment! Please leave immediately!

00:19:22.427 --> 00:19:25.597
It appears it wasn't an accident! It's the XAT!

00:19:25.597 --> 00:19:28.667
Meaning there must be a Demoniac!

00:19:28.667 --> 00:19:31.170
I've just confirmed it! It's a Demoniac!

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.832
It appears to have a hostage!

00:20:24.756 --> 00:20:28.760
I'm not sure what happened, but
it seems the Demoniac was beaten

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:36.301
not by the XAT, but by this person
who showed up on a motorcycle!

00:20:36.301 --> 00:20:39.338
It can't be!

00:20:39.338 --> 00:20:41.907
However, after he rammed
into it with his motorcycle,

00:20:41.907 --> 00:20:43.775
he moved so fast that we couldn't keep up!

00:20:43.775 --> 00:20:45.510
Just how did he manage to...?!

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.247
Gerd Frentzen...

00:20:48.247 --> 00:20:49.581
Who?

00:20:49.581 --> 00:20:52.017
This can't be for real...

00:20:52.017 --> 00:20:53.678
Hermann...

00:20:56.021 --> 00:20:58.285
Gerd...

00:21:47.439 --> 00:21:55.314
The ever-flowing songs search my memory

00:21:55.314 --> 00:22:07.426
The pain etched out by the
times slowly brings me back

00:22:07.426 --> 00:22:10.462
Embrace the sadness

00:22:10.462 --> 00:22:17.903
I know, the days that have passed by

00:22:17.903 --> 00:22:22.407
When I look up, it doesn't spill down

00:22:22.407 --> 00:22:28.980
As it trickles down the window,
sad rain rattles the heated isolation

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:34.353
Tonight I will be forsaken by sleep

00:22:34.353 --> 00:22:42.361
It's almost as if I'm traveling
to a country no one's ever heard of

00:22:42.361 --> 00:22:48.500
I'm all alone, and my words
don't get through to anyone

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:50.569
Wow wow

00:22:50.569 --> 00:22:58.577
Now my heart is frozen and waiting

00:22:58.577 --> 00:23:05.574
because it wants a phone
call so it can connect with you

00:23:12.924 --> 00:23:15.527
The shattered pride of the past.

00:23:15.527 --> 00:23:20.832
When the pieces are put together
again, he's no longer who he was.

00:23:20.832 --> 00:23:24.403
Episode 2: "The Price of Glory."

00:23:24.403 --> 00:23:28.863
The monster in the mirror asks, "Who are you?"
